window.LAB = [{"title":"Set up your tools","icon":"🧰","time":"30 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Every DevOps project starts the same way: the right tools on your machine and a <strong>safe</strong> AWS account. In this lab you'll rebuild the Memos platform from nothing, the same way the real repo was built.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🔧 <strong>How the lab works:</strong> each step explains <strong>what</strong> and <strong>why</strong>, then gives you a command to type into the practice terminal. You can tap <strong>Run it for me</strong> on your phone. To do it for real, copy the commands into your own terminal.</p>\n</blockquote>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  L[\"💻 laptop<br/>git · docker · aws · terraform\"] --> GH[GitHub repo]\n  GH --> AWS[\"☁️ AWS: VPC · ALB · ECS · ECR\"]\n  AWS --> W[\"🌐 tm.myegh.com\"]","caption":"Where we're heading"}],"steps":[{"title":"Install Git and check it","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Git tracks every change to your code. On macOS run <code>brew install git</code>; on Ubuntu <code>sudo apt install -y git</code>.</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"git --version","output":"git version 2.47.1"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Tell Git who you are, once per machine:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"git config --global user.name \"Enamul Rahman\"","output":"(no output means it worked)"}]},{"title":"Install Docker","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Docker builds and runs containers. Install <strong>Docker Desktop</strong> (Mac/Windows) or Docker Engine (Linux), then check:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"docker run --rm hello-world","output":"Unable to find image 'hello-world:latest' locally\nlatest: Pulling from library/hello-world\nStatus: Downloaded newer image for hello-world:latest\n\nHello from Docker!\nThis message shows that your installation appears to be working correctly."},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>What did <code>docker run --rm hello-world</code> just do?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Built an image from a Dockerfile","ok":false},{"t":"Pulled an image from Docker Hub, ran it as a container, then removed the container (<code>--rm</code>)","ok":true},{"t":"Installed Docker","ok":false},{"t":"Pushed an image to ECR","ok":false}],"explain":"<p><code>run</code> = pull if missing → create → start. <code>--rm</code> cleans up the container when it exits.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Install the AWS CLI and Terraform","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The <strong>AWS CLI</strong> talks to AWS's APIs from your terminal. <strong>Terraform</strong> turns <code>.tf</code> files into real infrastructure. On macOS: <code>brew install awscli hashicorp/tap/terraform</code>.</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"aws --version","output":"aws-cli/2.22.4 Python/3.12.6 Darwin/24.1.0 source/arm64"},{"type":"term","cmd":"terraform -version","output":"Terraform v1.13.5\non darwin_arm64"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>⚠️ Match the pipeline's version (Memos pins <strong>1.13.5</strong>), so local and CI behave the same.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"Secure the AWS account","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>In the AWS console, as root, do these <strong>once</strong>:\n1. Turn on <strong>MFA</strong> for the root user.\n2. <strong>Billing → Budgets →</strong> create a monthly budget (e.g. $20) with email alerts.\n3. Enable <strong>IAM Identity Center</strong> and create an admin user for yourself.\n4. Sign out of root and never use it day to day.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  ROOT[\"root user<br/>🔒 MFA · no keys · locked away\"] -.only for billing/emergencies.-> ACC[(AWS account)]\n  YOU[\"you via IAM Identity Center<br/>short-lived credentials\"] --> ACC"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why create a separate admin identity instead of using the root user?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Root can't use the CLI","ok":false},{"t":"Root has unlimited, unrestrictable power, so if it's compromised you lose the account; day-to-day work should use a separate, revocable identity","ok":true},{"t":"Identity Center is required for Terraform","ok":false},{"t":"It's cheaper","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Least privilege starts with you. Keep root locked away behind MFA.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Log in from the terminal","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Use <strong>SSO</strong> so your laptop gets short-lived credentials, not access keys stored in a file.</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"aws configure sso","output":"SSO session name: memos\nSSO start URL: https://d-1234567890.awsapps.com/start\nSSO region: eu-west-1\nAttempting to automatically open the SSO authorization page in your default browser.\nSuccessfully logged into Start URL: https://d-1234567890.awsapps.com/start\nCLI default client Region [None]: eu-west-1\nProfile name: memos"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Then check who you are:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"aws sts get-caller-identity --profile memos","output":"{\n    \"UserId\": \"AROA3XFRBF23EXAMPLE:enamul\",\n    \"Account\": \"123456789012\",\n    \"Arn\": \"arn:aws:sts::123456789012:assumed-role/AWSReservedSSO_AdministratorAccess_ab12/enamul\"\n}"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>🔧 Run <code>export AWS_PROFILE=memos</code> so every later command uses this login.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]}]},{"title":"Create the repo and get the app","icon":"📁","time":"15 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The infrastructure lives in its own repository, <strong>memos-aws-infra</strong>, with the Memos source code in an <code>app/</code> folder.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart TB\n  R[memos-aws-infra/] --> A[\"app/ (Memos source)\"]\n  R --> D[Dockerfile]\n  R --> B[\"bootstrap/ (state + OIDC)\"]\n  R --> I[\"infra/ (main stack + modules)\"]\n  R --> W[\".github/workflows/\"]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Create the repository","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"mkdir memos-aws-infra && cd memos-aws-infra && git init","output":"Initialized empty Git repository in /Users/enamul/memos-aws-infra/.git/"}]},{"title":"Bring in the Memos source","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Copy the open-source app into <code>app/</code>. A shallow clone is enough, and you remove its <code>.git</code> so it becomes plain files in your repo.</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/usememos/memos.git app && rm -rf app/.git","output":"Cloning into 'app'...\nremote: Enumerating objects: 1520, done.\nReceiving objects: 100% (1520/1520), 3.21 MiB | 9.80 MiB/s, done."}]},{"title":"Write a .gitignore (carefully)","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Keep build output, secrets and Terraform's local files out of Git.</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"gitignore","code":".terraform/\n*.tfstate\n*.tfstate.*\n*.tfplan\n.env\n/memos","file":".gitignore","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/.gitignore"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>🔧 <strong>The real bug:</strong> an earlier version said <code>memos</code> (no slash). That also matched <code>app/cmd/memos/</code>, so <code>main.go</code> was never committed and CI failed. <strong><code>/memos</code></strong> only matches at the repo root.</p>\n</blockquote>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why does <code>/memos</code> in .gitignore behave differently from <code>memos</code>?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"It doesn't: they're identical","ok":false},{"t":"A leading <code>/</code> anchors the pattern to the repo root, so it only ignores a top-level <code>memos</code>, not every file or folder named memos","ok":true},{"t":"<code>/memos</code> ignores folders only","ok":false},{"t":"<code>/memos</code> is invalid syntax","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Unanchored patterns match at <strong>any depth</strong>. That's how <code>cmd/memos/</code> disappeared.</p>"}}]},{"title":"First commit and push","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Create an empty repo on GitHub called <strong>memos-aws-infra</strong>, then:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"git add . && git commit -m \"Add Memos source\" && git push -u origin main","output":"[main (root-commit) 1a2b3c4] Add Memos source\n 1203 files changed, 98211 insertions(+)\nTo github.com:EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra.git\n * [new branch]      main -> main"}]}]},{"title":"Containerise Memos","icon":"🐳","time":"40 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>You'll package Memos into a small, secure image with a <strong>three-stage</strong> Dockerfile, then run it locally.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  F[\"① frontend<br/>node:22-alpine\"] -->|dist/| B[\"② backend<br/>golang:1.25-alpine<br/>static binary\"]\n  B -->|/memos| R[\"③ runtime<br/>alpine:3.21 · user 1001 · :8081\"]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Stage 1: build the frontend","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The React frontend compiles into static files. Copy the <strong>lock files first</strong> so dependency installs are cached between builds.</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"dockerfile","code":"FROM node:22-alpine AS frontend\nWORKDIR /build/web\nRUN npm install --global pnpm@10.24.0\nCOPY app/web/package.json app/web/pnpm-lock.yaml ./\nRUN pnpm install --frozen-lockfile\nCOPY app/web/ ./\nRUN pnpm release","file":"Dockerfile"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why copy <code>package.json</code> and the lock file <strong>before</strong> the rest of the frontend source?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"npm requires it","ok":false},{"t":"So the slow <code>pnpm install</code> layer is cached and only re-runs when dependencies change, not on every code edit","ok":true},{"t":"To make the image smaller","ok":false},{"t":"So the files are owned by root","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Order layers from least- to most-frequently changing.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Stage 2: compile the Go backend","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p><code>CGO_ENABLED=0</code> makes a <strong>static</strong> binary with no C libraries needed. <code>-ldflags=\"-s -w\"</code> strips debug info.</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"dockerfile","code":"FROM golang:1.25-alpine AS backend\nWORKDIR /build\nRUN apk add --no-cache git ca-certificates\nCOPY app/go.mod app/go.sum ./\nRUN go mod download\nCOPY app/ ./\nCOPY --from=frontend /build/server/router/frontend/dist ./server/router/frontend/dist\nRUN CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -trimpath -ldflags=\"-s -w\" -tags netgo,osusergo -o /memos ./cmd/memos","file":"Dockerfile"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>🔧 <strong>Story 3:</strong> the image was <code>golang:1.23</code>, but <code>go.mod</code> needed newer Go. It's now <strong>1.25</strong>, matching the code. Always match toolchain versions.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"Stage 3: a tiny, non-root runtime","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Only the binary, CA certificates and time-zone data. A dedicated user, <strong>1001</strong>, owns the data folder.</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"dockerfile","code":"FROM alpine:3.21 AS runtime\nRUN apk add --no-cache ca-certificates tzdata && \\\n    addgroup -S -g 1001 appuser && \\\n    adduser -S -D -u 1001 -G appuser appuser && \\\n    mkdir -p /var/opt/memos && chown appuser:appuser /var/opt/memos\nCOPY --from=backend /memos /usr/local/bin/memos\nWORKDIR /var/opt/memos\nENV MEMOS_PORT=8081 MEMOS_DATA=/var/opt/memos\nUSER 1001:1001\nEXPOSE 8081\nENTRYPOINT [\"memos\"]","file":"Dockerfile"}]},{"title":"Build the image","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p><code>--platform linux/amd64</code> matches Fargate's default CPU architecture, even if you're on an ARM Mac.</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"docker build --platform linux/amd64 -t memos:dev .","output":"[+] Building 212.4s (24/24) FINISHED\n => [frontend 5/6] RUN pnpm install --frozen-lockfile           58.1s\n => [backend 7/7] RUN CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -trimpath ...      96.3s\n => [runtime 3/3] COPY --from=backend /memos /usr/local/bin/memos 0.1s\n => naming to docker.io/library/memos:dev"},{"type":"term","cmd":"docker images memos","output":"REPOSITORY   TAG       IMAGE ID       CREATED          SIZE\nmemos        dev       4f1c9a2b7e3d   10 seconds ago   75.8MB"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>🔧 A single-stage build of the same code was <strong>2.79 GB</strong>. That's about 97% smaller.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"Run it and test it","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Publish container port 8081 on your laptop and give it a volume so the data survives restarts.</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"docker run -d --name memos -p 8081:8081 -v memos-data:/var/opt/memos memos:dev","output":"9b3e0c1d77f2a8c4e1f6a3b5d9e8c7f0a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6"},{"type":"term","cmd":"curl -i http://localhost:8081/healthz","output":"HTTP/1.1 200 OK\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\n\nService ready."},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Open <strong>http://localhost:8081</strong> in a browser and you'll see Memos running locally.</p>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Which user is the Memos process running as inside the container?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"root","ok":false},{"t":"UID 1001 (appuser)","ok":true},{"t":"nobody","ok":false},{"t":"the same user as your laptop","ok":false}],"explain":"<p><code>USER 1001:1001</code> in the Dockerfile. If the app were compromised, the attacker wouldn't be root.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Commit the Dockerfile","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"git add Dockerfile .dockerignore && git commit -m \"Add multi-stage Dockerfile\" && git push","output":"[main 5d6e7f8] Add multi-stage Dockerfile\n 2 files changed, 41 insertions(+)"}]}]},{"title":"Bootstrap: state bucket and OIDC","icon":"🪣","time":"30 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Before the main infrastructure, you need two <strong>long-lived</strong> things: a place to store Terraform state, and a keyless identity for GitHub Actions. They live in their own <code>bootstrap/</code> stack.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  subgraph BOOT[\"bootstrap/ · local state · run once\"]\n    S3[(\"S3: memos-terraform-state-enamul<br/>versioned · encrypted · private\")]\n    OIDC[\"IAM OIDC provider<br/>token.actions.githubusercontent.com\"]\n    ROLE[\"IAM role github-actions-role\"]\n  end\n  GHA[GitHub Actions] -->|\"AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity\"| ROLE"}],"steps":[{"title":"Provider configuration","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"terraform {\n  required_version = \">= 1.10.0, < 2.0.0\"\n  required_providers {\n    aws = { source = \"hashicorp/aws\", version = \"~> 5.0\" }\n  }\n}\n\nprovider \"aws\" {\n  region = \"eu-west-1\"\n  default_tags {\n    tags = { Project = \"Memos\", ManagedBy = \"Terraform\" }\n  }\n}","file":"bootstrap/provider.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/bootstrap/provider.tf"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p><code>default_tags</code> stamps every resource, which makes cost reports and clean-up easy.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"The state bucket","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_s3_bucket\" \"state\" {\n  bucket = \"memos-terraform-state-enamul\"   # globally unique: use your own\n  lifecycle { prevent_destroy = true }\n}\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_versioning\" \"state\" {\n  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.state.id\n  versioning_configuration { status = \"Enabled\" }\n}\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_server_side_encryption_configuration\" \"state\" {\n  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.state.id\n  rule {\n    apply_server_side_encryption_by_default {\n      sse_algorithm = \"AES256\"\n    }\n  }\n}\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block\" \"state\" {\n  bucket                  = aws_s3_bucket.state.id\n  block_public_acls       = true\n  block_public_policy     = true\n  ignore_public_acls      = true\n  restrict_public_buckets = true\n}","file":"bootstrap/state.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/bootstrap/state.tf"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Plus a bucket policy that <strong>denies any request not using HTTPS</strong> (<code>aws:SecureTransport = false</code>).</p>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>What does <code>prevent_destroy = true</code> protect against?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Someone deleting objects in the bucket","ok":false},{"t":"Terraform destroying the bucket, even when running <code>terraform destroy</code>","ok":true},{"t":"Public access to the bucket","ok":false},{"t":"Encryption being turned off","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>It's a Terraform safety catch. Versioning protects the <strong>objects</strong> inside.</p>"}}]},{"title":"The OIDC provider and role","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>GitHub signs a token for each workflow run. AWS trusts that token <strong>only</strong> for your repo.</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_iam_openid_connect_provider\" \"github\" {\n  url            = \"https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\"\n  client_id_list = [\"sts.amazonaws.com\"]\n  thumbprint_list = [\"ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff\"]\n}\n\nresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"github_actions\" {\n  name = \"github-actions-role\"\n  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    Statement = [{\n      Effect    = \"Allow\"\n      Principal = { Federated = aws_iam_openid_connect_provider.github.arn }\n      Action    = \"sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity\"\n      Condition = {\n        StringEquals = { \"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:aud\" = \"sts.amazonaws.com\" }\n        StringLike   = { \"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:sub\" = \"repo:EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra:*\" }\n      }\n    }]\n  })\n}","file":"bootstrap/oidc.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/bootstrap/oidc.tf"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>⚠️ The real repo attaches <strong>AdministratorAccess</strong> to this role, which is simple but too broad. In stage 15 you'll tighten it.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"Apply the bootstrap","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"cd bootstrap && terraform init","output":"Initializing provider plugins...\n- Installing hashicorp/aws v5.82.2...\nTerraform has been successfully initialized!"},{"type":"term","cmd":"terraform apply","output":"Plan: 8 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy.\n\nDo you want to perform these actions?\n  Enter a value: yes\n\naws_s3_bucket.state: Creation complete after 2s [id=memos-terraform-state-enamul]\naws_iam_openid_connect_provider.github: Creation complete after 1s\naws_iam_role.github_actions: Creation complete after 1s [id=github-actions-role]\n\nApply complete! Resources: 8 added, 0 changed, 0 destroyed."}]},{"title":"Give GitHub the role ARN","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>In GitHub: <strong>Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → New secret</strong> named <code>AWS_ROLE_ARN</code>, with the role's ARN as the value.</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"aws iam get-role --role-name github-actions-role --query Role.Arn --output text","output":"arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/github-actions-role"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Is the role ARN a sensitive credential?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Yes, it's as dangerous as an access key","ok":false},{"t":"Not really: it's an identifier; only workflows matching the trust policy can assume it. It's stored as a secret mainly for tidiness","ok":true},{"t":"Yes, anyone with it can log in to AWS","ok":false},{"t":"It expires after an hour","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>The protection is the <strong>trust policy</strong> (<code>aud</code> + <code>sub</code>), not the secrecy of the ARN.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"Terraform skeleton for the main stack","icon":"🏗️","time":"20 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Now the main stack in <code>infra/</code>. Its state lives in the bucket you just created.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart TB\n  P[provider.tf<br/>backend s3 + lockfile] --> M[main.tf<br/>calls 7 modules]\n  V[variables.tf] --> M\n  T[terraform.tfvars<br/>real values] --> V\n  M --> O[outputs.tf]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Backend and provider","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"terraform {\n  required_version = \">= 1.10.0, < 2.0.0\"\n  required_providers {\n    aws = { source = \"hashicorp/aws\", version = \"~> 5.0\" }\n  }\n  backend \"s3\" {\n    bucket       = \"memos-terraform-state-enamul\"\n    key          = \"prod/terraform.tfstate\"\n    region       = \"eu-west-1\"\n    encrypt      = true\n    use_lockfile = true      # S3 native locking (Terraform 1.10+)\n  }\n}\n\nprovider \"aws\" {\n  region = var.aws_region\n  default_tags { tags = { Project = \"Memos\", ManagedBy = \"Terraform\" } }\n}","file":"infra/provider.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/provider.tf"}]},{"title":"Variables and values","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Declare inputs in <code>variables.tf</code>, and put the real values in <code>terraform.tfvars</code>:</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"project_name = \"memos\"\nenvironment  = \"prod\"\naws_region   = \"eu-west-1\"\ndomain_name  = \"myegh.com\"\n\nvpc_cidr             = \"10.0.0.0/16\"\npublic_subnet_cidrs  = [\"10.0.1.0/24\", \"10.0.2.0/24\"]\nprivate_subnet_cidrs = [\"10.0.3.0/24\", \"10.0.4.0/24\"]\navailability_zones   = [\"eu-west-1a\", \"eu-west-1b\"]\n\nrepository_name = \"memos\"","file":"infra/terraform.tfvars","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/terraform.tfvars"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p><code>image_url</code> has a default of <code>\"\"</code> and is passed in by the pipeline with each deploy.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"Initialise with the remote backend","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"cd ../infra && terraform init","output":"Initializing the backend...\nSuccessfully configured the backend \"s3\"! Terraform will automatically\nuse this backend unless the backend configuration changes.\nInitializing modules...\nTerraform has been successfully initialized!"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Where will this stack's state be stored?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"In <code>infra/terraform.tfstate</code> on your laptop","ok":false},{"t":"In S3 at <code>memos-terraform-state-enamul/prod/terraform.tfstate</code>, locked with a <code>.tflock</code> object","ok":true},{"t":"In GitHub","ok":false},{"t":"In DynamoDB","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Shared by you and CI, versioned, encrypted, and locked during applies.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"Build the network","icon":"🏘️","time":"30 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>A VPC across two AZs, with public subnets for the load balancer and NAT, and private subnets for the app.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart TB\n  I((Internet)) <--> IGW[Internet gateway]\n  subgraph VPC[\"VPC 10.0.0.0/16\"]\n    subgraph A[\"eu-west-1a\"]\n      PA[\"public 10.0.1.0/24<br/>NAT-a\"] \n      RA[\"private 10.0.3.0/24\"]\n    end\n    subgraph B[\"eu-west-1b\"]\n      PB[\"public 10.0.2.0/24<br/>NAT-b\"]\n      RB[\"private 10.0.4.0/24\"]\n    end\n  end\n  IGW <--> PA & PB\n  RA -->|0.0.0.0/0| PA\n  RB -->|0.0.0.0/0| PB"}],"steps":[{"title":"VPC and subnets","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_vpc\" \"main\" {\n  cidr_block           = var.vpc_cidr\n  enable_dns_hostnames = true\n  enable_dns_support   = true\n}\n\nresource \"aws_subnet\" \"public\" {\n  count             = length(var.public_subnet_cidrs)\n  vpc_id            = aws_vpc.main.id\n  cidr_block        = var.public_subnet_cidrs[count.index]\n  availability_zone = data.aws_availability_zones.available.names[count.index]\n}\n\nresource \"aws_subnet\" \"private\" {\n  count             = length(var.private_subnet_cidrs)\n  vpc_id            = aws_vpc.main.id\n  cidr_block        = var.private_subnet_cidrs[count.index]\n  availability_zone = data.aws_availability_zones.available.names[count.index]\n}","file":"infra/modules/vpc/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/modules/vpc/main.tf"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p><code>count</code> creates one subnet per CIDR in the list, and each lands in a different AZ.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"Internet gateway and NAT gateways","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>One NAT gateway <strong>per AZ</strong>, each with its own Elastic IP, so one AZ failing doesn't cut off the other's outbound traffic.</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_internet_gateway\" \"main\" { vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id }\n\nresource \"aws_eip\" \"nat\" {\n  count  = length(var.public_subnet_cidrs)\n  domain = \"vpc\"\n}\n\nresource \"aws_nat_gateway\" \"main\" {\n  count         = length(var.public_subnet_cidrs)\n  allocation_id = aws_eip.nat[count.index].id\n  subnet_id     = aws_subnet.public[count.index].id\n  depends_on    = [aws_internet_gateway.main]\n}","file":"infra/modules/vpc/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/modules/vpc/main.tf"}]},{"title":"Route tables","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The public route table sends internet traffic to the <strong>IGW</strong>. Each private route table sends it to <strong>its own AZ's NAT</strong>.</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_route_table\" \"public\" {\n  vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id\n  route {\n    cidr_block = \"0.0.0.0/0\"\n    gateway_id = aws_internet_gateway.main.id\n  }\n}\n\nresource \"aws_route_table\" \"private\" {\n  count  = length(var.private_subnet_cidrs)\n  vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id\n  route {\n    cidr_block     = \"0.0.0.0/0\"\n    nat_gateway_id = aws_nat_gateway.main[count.index].id\n  }\n}","file":"infra/modules/vpc/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/modules/vpc/main.tf"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>What makes <code>10.0.1.0/24</code> a <strong>public</strong> subnet?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Its CIDR range","ok":false},{"t":"It's in AZ a","ok":false},{"t":"Its route table sends <code>0.0.0.0/0</code> to the internet gateway","ok":true},{"t":"It has a NAT gateway","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>\"Public\" is defined by the <strong>route</strong>, not a setting.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Call the module and apply","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"module \"vpc\" {\n  source               = \"./modules/vpc\"\n  project_name         = var.project_name\n  environment          = var.environment\n  vpc_cidr             = var.vpc_cidr\n  public_subnet_cidrs  = var.public_subnet_cidrs\n  private_subnet_cidrs = var.private_subnet_cidrs\n  availability_zones   = var.availability_zones\n}","file":"infra/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/main.tf"},{"type":"term","cmd":"terraform apply -target=module.vpc","output":"Plan: 15 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy.\nmodule.vpc.aws_vpc.main: Creation complete after 2s [id=vpc-0a1b2c3d4e5f67890]\nmodule.vpc.aws_nat_gateway.main[0]: Still creating... [1m30s elapsed]\nmodule.vpc.aws_nat_gateway.main[1]: Creation complete after 1m44s\nApply complete! Resources: 15 added, 0 changed, 0 destroyed."},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>⚠️ <code>-target</code> is handy while learning, building one piece at a time. Day to day, run plain <code>plan</code>/<code>apply</code> so the whole stack stays consistent. NAT gateways now cost money every hour, so <code>terraform destroy</code> at the end of a session if you're practising.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]}]},{"title":"Security groups","icon":"🔒","time":"15 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Two firewalls: one for the ALB (open to the world on 80/443) and one for the tasks (open <strong>only</strong> to the ALB, on 8081).</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  W((Internet)) -->|80, 443| ALB[ALB SG]\n  ALB -->|8081| ECS[ECS SG]\n  ECS -->|443| OUT((\"ECR, S3, Logs<br/>via NAT\"))"}],"steps":[{"title":"Two empty groups","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_security_group\" \"alb\" {\n  name   = \"${var.project_name}-${var.environment}-alb-sg\"\n  vpc_id = var.vpc_id\n}\nresource \"aws_security_group\" \"ecs\" {\n  name   = \"${var.project_name}-${var.environment}-ecs-sg\"\n  vpc_id = var.vpc_id\n}","file":"infra/modules/security/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/modules/security/main.tf"}]},{"title":"Rules as separate resources","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Separate rule resources are easier to read and change than inline blocks. Note the <strong>SG-to-SG</strong> references:</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_vpc_security_group_ingress_rule\" \"alb_https\" {\n  security_group_id = aws_security_group.alb.id\n  cidr_ipv4         = \"0.0.0.0/0\"\n  ip_protocol       = \"tcp\"\n  from_port         = 443\n  to_port           = 443\n}\nresource \"aws_vpc_security_group_egress_rule\" \"alb_to_ecs\" {\n  security_group_id            = aws_security_group.alb.id\n  referenced_security_group_id = aws_security_group.ecs.id\n  ip_protocol = \"tcp\"\n  from_port   = 8081\n  to_port     = 8081\n}\nresource \"aws_vpc_security_group_ingress_rule\" \"ecs_from_alb\" {\n  security_group_id            = aws_security_group.ecs.id\n  referenced_security_group_id = aws_security_group.alb.id\n  ip_protocol = \"tcp\"\n  from_port   = 8081\n  to_port     = 8081\n}\nresource \"aws_vpc_security_group_egress_rule\" \"ecs_https\" {\n  security_group_id = aws_security_group.ecs.id\n  cidr_ipv4         = \"0.0.0.0/0\"\n  ip_protocol       = \"tcp\"\n  from_port         = 443\n  to_port           = 443\n}","file":"infra/modules/security/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/modules/security/main.tf"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>There's also a port-80 ingress rule on the ALB, used only for the HTTPS redirect.</p>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>What would break if you deleted the <code>alb_to_ecs</code> <strong>egress</strong> rule?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Nothing: security groups are stateful","ok":false},{"t":"The ALB couldn't open connections to the tasks on 8081, so health checks fail and users get errors","ok":true},{"t":"Only HTTPS would break","ok":false},{"t":"The NAT gateway would stop","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Stateful means <strong>replies</strong> are allowed automatically. The ALB still needs an egress rule to <strong>start</strong> connections to the targets.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"ECR and your first image push","icon":"📦","time":"20 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Create the private registry, then push the image you built in stage 3.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  L[\"💻 memos:dev\"] -->|docker tag| T[\"…/memos:3f9c2e1…\"] -->|docker push| ECR[(\"ECR memos<br/>IMMUTABLE · scan on push\")]"}],"steps":[{"title":"The repository","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_ecr_repository\" \"this\" {\n  name                 = var.repository_name\n  image_tag_mutability = \"IMMUTABLE\"\n  force_delete         = true\n  image_scanning_configuration { scan_on_push = true }\n}","file":"infra/modules/ecr/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/modules/ecr/main.tf"},{"type":"term","cmd":"terraform apply -target=module.ecr","output":"module.ecr.aws_ecr_repository.this: Creation complete after 1s [id=memos]\nApply complete! Resources: 1 added, 0 changed, 0 destroyed."}]},{"title":"Log Docker in to ECR","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"aws ecr get-login-password | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin 123456789012.dkr.ecr.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com","output":"Login Succeeded"}]},{"title":"Tag with the commit SHA and push","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"docker tag memos:dev 123456789012.dkr.ecr.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/memos:$(git rev-parse HEAD)","output":"(no output means it worked)"},{"type":"term","cmd":"docker push 123456789012.dkr.ecr.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/memos:$(git rev-parse HEAD)","output":"The push refers to repository [123456789012.dkr.ecr.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/memos]\n5f70bf18a086: Pushed\n3f9c2e1d…: digest: sha256:9a8b7c… size: 1157"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>You run the same <code>docker push</code> again. What happens?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"It overwrites the old image","ok":false},{"t":"ECR rejects it: the tag already exists and tags are immutable","ok":true},{"t":"It creates <code>memos:sha-2</code>","ok":false},{"t":"It deletes the old image first","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>That's the \"re-run\" problem <code>build.yml</code> solves by checking ECR first and reusing the image.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"DNS and the certificate","icon":"🔐","time":"20 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Look up your Route 53 hosted zone, then request an ACM certificate that Terraform validates automatically.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"sequenceDiagram\n  participant TF as Terraform\n  participant ACM\n  participant R53 as Route 53\n  TF->>ACM: request cert (myegh.com + tm.myegh.com)\n  ACM-->>TF: validation CNAMEs\n  TF->>R53: create the CNAMEs\n  ACM->>R53: check\n  ACM-->>TF: ISSUED ✅"}],"steps":[{"title":"Find the hosted zone","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The domain is already registered and its hosted zone exists, so Terraform just <strong>looks it up</strong> with a data source:</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"data \"aws_route53_zone\" \"main\" {\n  name         = var.domain_name\n  private_zone = false\n}","file":"infra/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/main.tf"},{"type":"term","cmd":"aws route53 list-hosted-zones-by-name --dns-name myegh.com --query \"HostedZones[0].Id\"","output":"\"/hostedzone/Z0123456789ABCDEFGHIJ\""}]},{"title":"Request and validate the certificate","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_acm_certificate\" \"this\" {\n  domain_name               = var.domain_name\n  subject_alternative_names = [\"tm.${var.domain_name}\"]\n  validation_method         = \"DNS\"\n  lifecycle { create_before_destroy = true }\n}\n\nresource \"aws_route53_record\" \"validation\" {\n  for_each = {\n    for o in aws_acm_certificate.this.domain_validation_options : o.domain_name => {\n      name = o.resource_record_name, type = o.resource_record_type, record = o.resource_record_value\n    }\n  }\n  zone_id = var.zone_id\n  name    = each.value.name\n  type    = each.value.type\n  records = [each.value.record]\n  ttl     = 60\n}\n\nresource \"aws_acm_certificate_validation\" \"this\" {\n  certificate_arn         = aws_acm_certificate.this.arn\n  validation_record_fqdns = [for r in aws_route53_record.validation : r.fqdn]\n}","file":"infra/modules/acm/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/modules/acm/main.tf"},{"type":"term","cmd":"terraform apply -target=module.acm","output":"module.acm.aws_acm_certificate.this: Creation complete after 9s\nmodule.acm.aws_route53_record.validation[\"myegh.com\"]: Creation complete after 35s\nmodule.acm.aws_route53_record.validation[\"tm.myegh.com\"]: Creation complete after 35s\nmodule.acm.aws_acm_certificate_validation.this: Still creating... [1m0s elapsed]\nmodule.acm.aws_acm_certificate_validation.this: Creation complete after 1m12s"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why <code>for_each</code> here rather than <code>count</code>?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"count doesn't work with Route 53","ok":false},{"t":"The validation options are keyed by domain name, so for_each gives stable keys that don't shift if a domain is added or removed","ok":true},{"t":"for_each is required by ACM","ok":false},{"t":"count would create duplicate certificates","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Stable keys mean stable resources.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"The load balancer","icon":"⚖️","time":"25 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The public front door: port 80 redirects, port 443 terminates TLS and forwards to the tasks on 8081.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  U((users)) --> L80[\":80\"] -->|301| L443[\":443 · ACM\"]\n  U --> L443 --> TG[\"target group · ip · 8081<br/>health check /\"] --> T[\"tasks\"]"}],"steps":[{"title":"ALB and target group","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_lb\" \"this\" {\n  name                       = \"${var.project_name}-alb\"\n  internal                   = false\n  load_balancer_type         = \"application\"\n  drop_invalid_header_fields = true\n  security_groups            = [var.security_group]\n  subnets                    = var.public_subnets\n}\n\nresource \"aws_lb_target_group\" \"this\" {\n  name        = \"${var.project_name}-tg\"\n  port        = 8081\n  protocol    = \"HTTP\"\n  vpc_id      = var.vpc_id\n  target_type = \"ip\"            # Fargate tasks register by IP\n  health_check {\n    path                = \"/\"\n    matcher             = \"200-399\"\n    interval            = 30\n    healthy_threshold   = 2\n    unhealthy_threshold = 2\n  }\n}","file":"infra/modules/alb/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/modules/alb/main.tf"}]},{"title":"Listeners: redirect and forward","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_lb_listener\" \"http\" {\n  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.this.arn\n  port              = 80\n  protocol          = \"HTTP\"\n  default_action {\n    type = \"redirect\"\n    redirect {\n      port        = \"443\"\n      protocol    = \"HTTPS\"\n      status_code = \"HTTP_301\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nresource \"aws_lb_listener\" \"https\" {\n  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.this.arn\n  port              = 443\n  protocol          = \"HTTPS\"\n  ssl_policy        = \"ELBSecurityPolicy-TLS13-1-2-2021-06\"\n  certificate_arn   = var.certificate_arn\n  default_action {\n    type             = \"forward\"\n    target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.this.arn\n  }\n}","file":"infra/modules/alb/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/modules/alb/main.tf"},{"type":"term","cmd":"terraform apply -target=module.alb","output":"module.alb.aws_lb.this: Still creating... [2m0s elapsed]\nmodule.alb.aws_lb.this: Creation complete after 2m31s\nApply complete! Resources: 4 added, 0 changed, 0 destroyed."},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why does the target group use <code>target_type = \"ip\"</code> for Fargate?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"The ALB only supports IP targets","ok":false},{"t":"Fargate has no EC2 instance to register; each task gets its own network interface and private IP (awsvpc mode), so targets are task IPs","ok":true},{"t":"IP targets are cheaper","ok":false},{"t":"It's needed for HTTPS","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>ALBs support instance, IP and Lambda targets. Fargate tasks are reached by their own IPs.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"IAM roles for ECS","icon":"🎭","time":"10 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Two roles with two different jobs.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  ECS[\"ECS agent\"] -->|assumes| ER[\"execution role<br/>pull ECR · write logs\"]\n  APP[\"Memos code\"] -->|assumes| TR[\"task role<br/>(no permissions)\"]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Trust ECS, then attach permissions","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"data \"aws_iam_policy_document\" \"ecs_assume_role_policy\" {\n  statement {\n    actions = [\"sts:AssumeRole\"]\n    principals {\n      type        = \"Service\"\n      identifiers = [\"ecs-tasks.amazonaws.com\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"execution_role\" {\n  name               = \"${var.project_name}-ecs-execution-role\"\n  assume_role_policy = data.aws_iam_policy_document.ecs_assume_role_policy.json\n}\nresource \"aws_iam_role_policy_attachment\" \"execution_policy\" {\n  role       = aws_iam_role.execution_role.name\n  policy_arn = \"arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonECSTaskExecutionRolePolicy\"\n}\n\nresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"task_role\" {\n  name               = \"${var.project_name}-ecs-task-role\"\n  assume_role_policy = data.aws_iam_policy_document.ecs_assume_role_policy.json\n}","file":"infra/modules/iam/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/modules/iam/main.tf"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Memos never calls AWS APIs itself. Which role can therefore have <strong>no</strong> permissions attached?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"The execution role","ok":false},{"t":"The task role","ok":true},{"t":"Both","ok":false},{"t":"Neither","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>The execution role still needs ECR pull and CloudWatch Logs permissions so ECS can start the task.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"Run Memos on ECS and go live","icon":"🚀","time":"30 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The final piece: a cluster, a task definition, a service wired to the ALB, and a DNS record. After this, <strong>tm.myegh.com</strong> is live.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart TB\n  U([User]) --> R53[Route 53 alias] --> ALB\n  subgraph VPC\n    ALB[ALB · public] -->|8081| T[Fargate task · private]\n  end\n  T --> ECR[(ECR)]\n  T --> CW[CloudWatch /ecs/memos]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Cluster and log group","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_ecs_cluster\" \"this\" {\n  name = \"${var.project_name}-cluster\"\n  setting {                       # cost trade-off\n    name  = \"containerInsights\"\n    value = \"disabled\"\n  }\n}\n\nresource \"aws_cloudwatch_log_group\" \"this\" {\n  name              = \"/ecs/${var.project_name}\"\n  retention_in_days = 7\n}","file":"infra/modules/ecs/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/modules/ecs/main.tf"}]},{"title":"The task definition","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_ecs_task_definition\" \"this\" {\n  family                   = \"${var.project_name}-task\"\n  requires_compatibilities = [\"FARGATE\"]\n  network_mode             = \"awsvpc\"\n  cpu                      = var.cpu          # 256 = 0.25 vCPU\n  memory                   = var.memory       # 512 MB\n  execution_role_arn       = var.execution_role_arn\n  task_role_arn            = var.task_role_arn\n  container_definitions = jsonencode([{\n    name         = \"memos\"\n    image        = var.image_url\n    essential    = true\n    portMappings = [{ containerPort = var.container_port, hostPort = var.container_port, protocol = \"tcp\" }]\n    logConfiguration = {\n      logDriver = \"awslogs\"\n      options = {\n        \"awslogs-group\"         = aws_cloudwatch_log_group.this.name\n        \"awslogs-region\"        = \"eu-west-1\"\n        \"awslogs-stream-prefix\" = \"ecs\"\n      }\n    }\n  }])\n}","file":"infra/modules/ecs/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/modules/ecs/main.tf"}]},{"title":"The service","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_ecs_service\" \"this\" {\n  name            = \"${var.project_name}-service\"\n  cluster         = aws_ecs_cluster.this.id\n  task_definition = aws_ecs_task_definition.this.arn\n  desired_count   = var.desired_count     # 1\n  launch_type     = \"FARGATE\"\n  network_configuration {\n    subnets          = var.private_subnet_ids\n    security_groups  = [var.ecs_security_group_id]\n    assign_public_ip = false\n  }\n  load_balancer {\n    target_group_arn = var.target_group_arn\n    container_name   = \"memos\"\n    container_port   = var.container_port\n  }\n}","file":"infra/modules/ecs/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/modules/ecs/main.tf"}]},{"title":"Point the domain at the ALB","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_route53_record\" \"app\" {\n  zone_id = data.aws_route53_zone.main.zone_id\n  name    = \"tm.${var.domain_name}\"\n  type    = \"A\"\n  alias {\n    name                   = module.alb.dns_name\n    zone_id                = module.alb.alb_zone_id\n    evaluate_target_health = true\n  }\n}","file":"infra/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/main.tf"}]},{"title":"Apply everything","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Now run a full plan and apply with the image you pushed:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"terraform apply -var=\"image_url=123456789012.dkr.ecr.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/memos:$(git rev-parse HEAD)\"","output":"Plan: 9 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy.\nmodule.ecs.aws_ecs_cluster.this: Creation complete after 11s\nmodule.ecs.aws_ecs_task_definition.this: Creation complete after 1s [id=memos-task]\nmodule.ecs.aws_ecs_service.this: Creation complete after 2s\naws_route53_record.app: Creation complete after 41s [id=Z0123…_tm.myegh.com_A]\n\nOutputs:\napp_url = \"https://tm.myegh.com\""}]},{"title":"Watch the service become healthy","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"aws ecs describe-services --cluster memos-cluster --services memos-service --query \"services[0].events[0:3].message\"","output":"[\n    \"(service memos-service) has reached a steady state.\",\n    \"(service memos-service) registered 1 targets in (target-group memos-tg)\",\n    \"(service memos-service) has started 1 tasks: (task 7d1e…).\"\n]"},{"type":"term","cmd":"curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\\n\" https://tm.myegh.com/healthz","output":"200"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>🎉 <strong>Memos is live on AWS.</strong></p>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>A user visits <code>http://tm.myegh.com</code>. Put the journey in order.</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"ECS → ALB → Route 53 → browser","ok":false},{"t":"Route 53 alias → ALB :80 → 301 to https → ALB :443 (TLS with ACM) → target group → task on 8081","ok":true},{"t":"NAT gateway → ECS → ALB","ok":false},{"t":"ACM → Route 53 → ECS","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Be able to say this in one breath. It's the most common \"explain your project\" question.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"Automate it with GitHub Actions","icon":"🔁","time":"45 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Everything so far was by hand. Now a push to <code>main</code> will build, scan, push and deploy automatically, with no stored AWS keys.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  P[push to main] --> B[\"build.yml<br/>tfsec · OIDC · build or reuse image\"] --> D[\"deploy.yml<br/>fmt · validate · plan · apply\"] --> H[\"curl /healthz\"]\n  M[manual] --> X[\"destroy.yml\"]"}],"steps":[{"title":"build.yml: triggers and permissions","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"name: Build and Push\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n    paths: ['app/**', 'Dockerfile', '.dockerignore']\n  workflow_dispatch:\nenv:\n  AWS_REGION: eu-west-1\n  ECR_REPOSITORY: memos\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions:\n      id-token: write     # allow OIDC\n      contents: read","file":".github/workflows/build.yml","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/.github/workflows/build.yml"}]},{"title":"build.yml: log in with OIDC","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - name: Scan Terraform security\n        uses: aquasecurity/tfsec-action@v1.0.3\n        with: { working_directory: infra }\n      - name: Configure AWS credentials\n        uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@v4\n        with:\n          role-to-assume: ${{ secrets.AWS_ROLE_ARN }}\n          aws-region: ${{ env.AWS_REGION }}\n      - id: login-ecr\n        uses: aws-actions/amazon-ecr-login@v2","file":".github/workflows/build.yml","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/.github/workflows/build.yml"}]},{"title":"build.yml: build or reuse the image","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Idempotent: if the SHA's image already exists, reuse it. Only <code>ImageNotFoundException</code> triggers a build, and any other error fails loudly.</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"      - name: Build or reuse image\n        env:\n          ECR_REGISTRY: ${{ steps.login-ecr.outputs.registry }}\n          IMAGE_TAG: ${{ github.sha }}\n        run: |\n          IMAGE=\"$ECR_REGISTRY/$ECR_REPOSITORY:$IMAGE_TAG\"\n          ERROR_FILE=$(mktemp)\n          if aws ecr describe-images --repository-name \"$ECR_REPOSITORY\" \\\n               --image-ids \"imageTag=$IMAGE_TAG\" > /dev/null 2>\"$ERROR_FILE\"; then\n            echo \"Image already exists; reusing $IMAGE\"\n          elif grep -q ImageNotFoundException \"$ERROR_FILE\"; then\n            docker build -t \"$IMAGE\" .\n            docker push \"$IMAGE\"\n          else\n            cat \"$ERROR_FILE\" >&2; exit 1\n          fi","file":".github/workflows/build.yml","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/.github/workflows/build.yml"}]},{"title":"deploy.yml: run after a successful build","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"name: Deploy\non:\n  workflow_run:\n    workflows: [\"Build and Push\"]\n    types: [completed]\n    branches: [main]\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      image_tag:\n        description: \"Full commit SHA of an existing ECR image\"\n        required: true\njobs:\n  deploy:\n    if: ${{ github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch' || github.event.workflow_run.conclusion == 'success' }}","file":".github/workflows/deploy.yml","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/.github/workflows/deploy.yml"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>The deploy job checks the SHA is 40 characters and exists in ECR, then runs <code>terraform fmt -check</code>, <code>init</code>, <code>validate</code>, <code>plan -out=tfplan</code> and <code>apply tfplan</code> with <code>image_url</code> set.</p>"}]},{"title":"deploy.yml: verify it worked","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"  health-check:\n    needs: deploy\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - run: sleep 60\n      - run: |\n          code=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" --max-time 30 https://tm.myegh.com/healthz)\n          if [ \"$code\" = \"200\" ]; then echo \"✅ Health check passed\"; else echo \"❌ got $code\"; exit 1; fi","file":".github/workflows/deploy.yml","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/.github/workflows/deploy.yml"}]},{"title":"Push and watch it run","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Make a small change in <code>app/</code> and push:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"git commit -am \"Tweak app title\" && git push","output":"[main 3f9c2e1] Tweak app title\nTo github.com:EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra.git\n   5d6e7f8..3f9c2e1  main -> main"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>In GitHub → <strong>Actions</strong>: <em>Build and Push</em> ✅ → <em>Deploy</em> ✅ → <em>Post Deploy Health Check</em> ✅.</p>"}]},{"title":"Practise a rollback","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>A bad version went out? <strong>Actions → Deploy → Run workflow</strong>, with <code>image_tag</code> set to the previous good SHA:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"gh workflow run deploy.yml -f image_tag=5d6e7f8a9b0c1d2e3f4a5b6c7d8e9f0a1b2c3d4e","output":"✓ Created workflow_dispatch event for deploy.yml at main"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why can you trust that this rollback deploys exactly the old code?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Terraform keeps old versions of the app","ok":false},{"t":"ECR tags are immutable, so that SHA tag can only ever point at the image built from that commit","ok":true},{"t":"GitHub caches old builds","ok":false},{"t":"ECS remembers old task definitions","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Immutable, SHA-tagged artefacts are what make rollbacks boring, and boring is good.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"Break it and fix it","icon":"🧯","time":"30 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The best way to learn troubleshooting is to cause real failures on purpose, then fix them. Try these on a practice environment, never on something real users depend on.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart TB\n  S([symptom]) --> D{\"502 / 503 / 504?\"}\n  D -->|503| E[\"ECS: task running?<br/>stopped reason\"]\n  D -->|502| L[\"logs: app crashing?<br/>wrong port?\"]\n  D -->|504 / timeout| N[\"SGs · routes · NACLs\"]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Drill 1: port drift","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Change <code>MEMOS_PORT</code> to <code>5230</code> in the Dockerfile (Memos' default) but leave everything else on 8081. Deploy.</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"aws elbv2 describe-target-health --target-group-arn arn:aws:elasticloadbalancing:eu-west-1:123456789012:targetgroup/memos-tg/abc123 --query \"TargetHealthDescriptions[0].TargetHealth\"","output":"{\n    \"State\": \"unhealthy\",\n    \"Reason\": \"Target.FailedHealthChecks\",\n    \"Description\": \"Health checks failed\"\n}"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>What's the fix that stops this ever happening again?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Open port 5230 in the security groups as well","ok":false},{"t":"Define the port once (a variable used by the image env, task definition, target group and SG rules) so they can't drift apart","ok":true},{"t":"Turn off health checks","ok":false},{"t":"Use port 80 everywhere","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>This was a real Memos bug: 5230 vs 8081. One source of truth for each value.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Drill 2: read the logs","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>When the task is crashing, the answer is usually in the logs:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"aws logs tail /ecs/memos --since 15m --follow","output":"2026-11-03T16:07:34 ecs/memos/7d1e… Memos 0.25.x started successfully!\n2026-11-03T16:07:34 ecs/memos/7d1e… Data directory: /var/opt/memos\n2026-11-03T16:07:34 ecs/memos/7d1e… Server running on port 8081"}]},{"title":"Drill 3: why did the task stop?","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"aws ecs describe-tasks --cluster memos-cluster --tasks 7d1e0c4b --query \"tasks[0].[stoppedReason,containers[0].exitCode]\"","output":"[\n    \"Essential container in task exited\",\n    137\n]"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Exit code 137 on this task most likely means…</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"the image wasn't found","ok":false},{"t":"the container was killed with SIGKILL, almost always for going over its 512 MB memory limit","ok":true},{"t":"a normal shutdown","ok":false},{"t":"a health check timeout","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>137 = 128 + 9. Raise the memory (a valid Fargate pair) and find out why usage grows.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Drill 4: drift","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Add an SSH rule to the ECS security group in the console, then:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"terraform plan -refresh-only","output":"Note: Objects have changed outside of Terraform\n  # module.security.aws_security_group.ecs has changed\nTerraform detected the following changes made outside of Terraform since the last apply."},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Remove the hand-made rule, and talk about <strong>why</strong> changes go through code.</p>"}]}]},{"title":"Level up: production improvements","icon":"🌟","time":"60 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The platform works. These upgrades turn it into something you'd defend in a senior interview. Each one matches a known limitation.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  A[RDS / EFS data tier] --> B[2+ tasks + autoscaling] --> C[circuit breaker + /healthz] --> D[least-privilege CI] --> E[plan on PR + approval]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Automatic rollback and a better health check","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_ecs_service\" \"this\" {\n  # …\n  health_check_grace_period_seconds = 60\n  deployment_circuit_breaker {\n    enable   = true\n    rollback = true\n  }\n}","file":"infra/modules/ecs/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/modules/ecs/main.tf"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"health_check {\n  path    = \"/healthz\"     # the real liveness endpoint\n  matcher = \"200\"\n}","file":"infra/modules/alb/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/modules/alb/main.tf"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>What does the circuit breaker add on top of the pipeline's <code>/healthz</code> check?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Faster image builds","ok":false},{"t":"ECS itself stops a failing rollout and returns to the last working deployment, with no human or pipeline needed","ok":true},{"t":"HTTPS","ok":false},{"t":"Auto scaling","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>The pipeline <strong>detects</strong> a bad deploy. The circuit breaker <strong>recovers</strong> from it.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Lock down the CI role","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Only <code>main</code> may assume the role, and with fewer permissions:</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"StringLike = {\n  \"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:sub\" = \"repo:EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra:ref:refs/heads/main\"\n}","file":"bootstrap/oidc.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/bootstrap/oidc.tf"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Then replace <code>AdministratorAccess</code> with a policy listing the ECR, ECS, ELB, EC2, IAM (scoped), ACM, Route 53, Logs and state-bucket actions Terraform actually uses. Pin third-party actions to commit SHAs while you're there.</p>"}]},{"title":"Move the data out of the container","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Memos supports Postgres. Add RDS in the private subnets and pass the DSN as a secret:</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"container_definitions = jsonencode([{\n  name  = \"memos\"\n  image = var.image_url\n  environment = [{ name = \"MEMOS_DRIVER\", value = \"postgres\" }]\n  secrets     = [{ name = \"MEMOS_DSN\", valueFrom = var.dsn_secret_arn }]\n  # …\n}])","file":"infra/modules/ecs/main.tf","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/infra/modules/ecs/main.tf"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Give the <strong>execution role</strong> <code>secretsmanager:GetSecretValue</code> on that secret, allow 5432 from the ECS SG to an RDS SG, and then <code>desired_count = 2</code>.</p>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>After moving to RDS, why is it now safe to run two tasks?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Fargate gives each task more memory","ok":false},{"t":"The tasks are stateless: both read and write the same database instead of their own local SQLite files","ok":true},{"t":"The ALB can now route to two targets","ok":false},{"t":"RDS makes tasks start faster","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Stateless app tier plus a shared, durable data tier: that's the pattern behind almost every scalable web app.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Plan on every pull request","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"on:\n  pull_request:\n    paths: ['infra/**']\njobs:\n  plan:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions: { id-token: write, contents: read, pull-requests: write }\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@v4\n        with: { role-to-assume: \"${{ secrets.AWS_PLAN_ROLE_ARN }}\", aws-region: eu-west-1 }\n      - uses: hashicorp/setup-terraform@v3\n      - run: terraform init && terraform plan -no-color | tee plan.txt\n        working-directory: infra","file":".github/workflows/plan.yml","href":"https://github.com/EnamulRahman/memos-aws-infra/blob/main/.github/workflows/plan.yml"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Post <code>plan.txt</code> as a PR comment, and require a reviewer on a protected <code>production</code> environment before <code>apply</code>. Reviewers see <strong>exactly</strong> what will change.</p>"}]}]}];
